		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: MD9600 with Open Firmware pre-loaded (USA)]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4415&amp;p=33004#p33004"><![CDATA[
Yes. CPU is made by ST Micro aka STM, or its a Chinese clone of the CPU.<br><br>Yes. There is an old way and a new way to interface with the DFU driver, depending on which driver has been installed.<br><br>Its the commands / interface between the Windows application (i.e the CPS) and the driver which has changed.<br><br>Just to complicate things, the CPU is actually running special firmware when the radio is in update mode, which mimics the built in DFU functionality of the silicon of the CPU, but TYT etc added some extra non-standard functionality.<br><br>And potentially the new STM DFU driver may not be able to handle the non-standard functionality that the old driver could handle, so it may never be possible to make the new DFU driver work with the upload mode of the CPU.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Sep 18, 2024 6:48 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
