		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4415&amp;p=33002#p33002"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: MD9600 with Open Firmware pre-loaded (USA)]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4415&amp;p=33002#p33002"><![CDATA[
Unfortunately most of the problems with installing the firmware for the first time have been caused by STM the CPU manufacturer having 2 different and incompatible DFU drivers.<br><br>We use the older DFU driver which had been used for about 10 years, and probably got superseded about 1 or 2 years ago.<br><br>Windows 10 still seems to load the older DFU driver.  Windows 11 mostly seems to load the new driver.<br><br>I'm not sure what possessed STM to make their 2 drivers incompable with the applications that use them.<br>Its not just us thats impacted, loads of other radios have the same problem.<br><br>I think Baofeng and TYT may include the older DFU driver with their installers, but I'm not sure whether this in breach of the driver license, hence why we don't do this.<br><br>Also even if we did install the driver, its possible that someone is already using the newer driver on their PC for an unrelated / non-radio product and would not be happy if we replaced the driver that worked for that other device.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Sep 18, 2024 4:17 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
